<title>PAKISTAN: Karachi port handles 114,053 tonnes cargo.</title>
<headline>Karachi port handles 114,053 tonnes cargo.</headline>
<dateline>KARACHI, Pakistan 1996-12-31</dateline>
<text>
<p>Pakistan's Karachi Port Trust said it had handled 114,053 tonnes of export and import cargo in the 24 hours to 7 a.m. (0200 GMT) on Tuesday compared to 92,644 tonnes in the same period on Monday.</p>
<p>Cargo handling in tonnes:</p>
<p>				    Tuesday     Dec 30</p>
<p>    Export cargo		20,017	28,776</p>
<p>    Import cargo		94,036	63,868</p>
<p>In the past 24 hours, three ships sailed and four berthed. In the next 24 hours, eight are expected to sail and 10 are expected to arrive.  </p>
<p>Berthing schedule of major vessels unloading or expected to unload at Karachi Port:</p>
<p>    Commodity	  Tonnes/TEUs  Ship		   Berthing</p>
<p>Gas oil		  35,000	 Rose bud	     31/12</p>
<p>Fertiliser	     30,100	 Eramus		 31/12</p>
<p>Fertiliser	     34,500	 Lucky Fortune	31/12</p>
<p>Palm oil		 18,000	 Wawasan Courage    01/01</p>
<p>Fertiliser	     31,406	 Asku		   01/01</p>
<p>High speed diesel    56,000	 Keefan		 02/01</p>
<p>Berthing schedule of major vessels unloading or expected to unload at the Karachi Port:</p>
<p>Commodity		Tonnes/TEUs  Ship	    Berthing</p>
<p>High speed diesel    56,000	 Keefen		 2/1</p>
<p>Palm oil		 18,000	 Wawasan Courage    1/1</p>
<p>High speed diesel    56,000	 Al-Maqwa	     due</p>
<p>Palm oil		 12,000	 Bunga Selasih    28/12</p>
<p>Gas oil		  35,000	 Rosebud		due</p>
<p>Chemical		  4,000	 Oriental Lily    26/12</p>
<p>Soyabean oil	    5,350	 Champion Trader  25/12</p>
<p>-- Karachi newsroom 9221-5685192</p>
</text>
